===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|vulgar|slang}} {{syn of|en|bullshit}} {{q|figurative senses}}.
#: {{syn|en|horsecrap|horsedung|;|''more at'' [[bullshit]]}}
## {{lb|en|vulgar|slang}} Serious [[harassment]] or abuse.
##: {{ux|en|That scumbag dumped a whole carload of '''horseshit''' over his associates.}}
## {{lb|en|vulgar|slang}} Blatant [[nonsense]], more likely stemming from ignorance than any intent to deceive.
##: {{ux|en|He thinks vinegar is alkaline? Don't you realize that's '''horseshit'''?}}
## {{lb|en|vulgar|slang}} Deliberate [[falsehood]]s ([[lie#Noun|lies]]); [[manipulation]]s or [[con#Noun|cons]] ([[fraud]]).
##: {{ux|en|He claims that he wasn't at that meeting? Don't you realize that's '''horseshit'''?}}
# {{lb|en|literally}} [[horse|Horse]] [[feces]] / [[manure]].
#: {{syn|en|horsecrap|horsedung}}
#: {{cot|en|q=livestock manures|bullshit|cowshit|goatshit|pigshit|sheepshit}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Gil Roscoe|title=Company of Thieves|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=qP0u_f4Wm04C|page=54|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=qP0u_f4Wm04C&dq=%22horseshit%22|passage=A huge one. It was my job to mix the '''horseshit''' in with the soil. Great big wheelbarrows full of '''horseshit'''. We used to drive around to farms that had horses and ask them if we could shovel up their '''horseshit'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Laurel Dewey|title=Betty's (Little Basement) Garden|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=d21Irx2h9y4C|page=253|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=d21Irx2h9y4C&pg=PA253&dq=%22horseshit%22|passage=The aroma was a mix of cedar, hay and '''horseshit''' but somehow, Betty found it pleasantly intoxicating.}}

